+- **section 6's diagnostics** (``route_07a``), on when the spec's ``instrument_07a`` is true (the default) and off when it
+  is false (Gate W0's third clause): pass-throughs at the module attribute ``_adaptive_levin_subregion`` (06c's, extended),
+  at the class attribute ``_Basis_SinCos.build_Levin_data`` and at the module attribute ``_sample_vectorized``, installed
+  for the timed section only (and, separately, around this harness's own re-solves after it), record every subregion
+  solve the driver makes in a call: its span, its caller's description (its role), whether it was forced to the nested
+  Clenshaw-Curtis pair, and for each build of its Levin data V as h's build_Levin_data returned it, 07's estimate
+  mean|theta'| * width computed from the same returned theta_prime_Cheb and grid by the parent's expression (dadd63a0's
+  build_Levin_data, verbatim), whether V took the node-partition sum (the module's own ``_changes_sign`` on the returned
+  theta_prime_Cheb, the test build_Levin_data makes), and the largest |theta| of the raw phase samples that build took
+  at the region's two ends (read from the samples _sample_vectorized returned, never evaluated again). After the call
+  each solve is classed by role (``own``: its span is a region the driver made, ``used_interval``, returned or later
+  bisected; else by its description: ``quarter``, a trust-check quarter; ``comparison_half``, a Levin leaf's
+  dataL/dataR; ``fallback_half``, a fallback leaf's halves; ``other``) and by whether its C2 route (V < SIX_PI against
+  the estimate < SIX_PI) or, both on the Levin route, its LU choice (> _LEVIN_DIRECT_SOLVE_PHASE_SPAN) differs; a forced
+  solve makes no such decision. Also: each non-forced Clenshaw-Curtis solve with a visited half that went to the Levin
+  solve, the smallest margins |V - 6 pi| and |V - 20 pi| among solves whose decision does not differ, and the
+  harness's own re-solves after the timed section (W3, the deep lines, the floor's terms, the declared terms, 06h's
